> problem here.

Magic traps could impose a soft cap onto how far one can push this.   
It happened to me that until midgame I hadn't a decent method of 
escape.  A no-port, no-dig level with magic trap could be a little 
tough even for better-prepared characters.  

On the other hand, this would make players a little more paranoid 
about traps in the mid-/end game, which could be a Good Thing.  

What I was thinking about was another idea, bleeding wounds.  That is, 
if a monster scores a good hit, you will not only suffer damage this 
round, but a smaller damage for several rounds.  This could also make 
monster mobs much more dangerous, and specific monsters with a 
particular high/long bleeding "ability" more fearsome, and increase 
the 'combat recovery' time which is ridicously short at the moment 
for a high-end character.  

